# Code owners for this repository.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners listed below on any pull request that
# touches the matching paths. This is advisory until branch protection for the
# default branch enables "Require review from Code Owners".

# goat-flow agent hooks are shell and Node scripts that run locally in a
# maintainer's coding-agent session, not in CI. A change here is a change to
# code that executes on a reviewer's machine as soon as they check the branch
# out, so it needs the same scrutiny as a release script.
/.goat-flow/hooks/ @Ardenexal

# Decides which .goat-flow/ paths are publishable at all. Loosening it can
# expose local session logs, plan contents, or the scratchpad.
/.goat-flow/.gitignore @Ardenexal

# CI configuration decides which checks run and therefore which of them can
# block a merge. The change-detection scripts in particular: a single path
# added to is_documentation() in changed-areas.sh, or one `if:` edited in
# pr.yml, can turn off up to fourteen required status checks, and in review it
# reads as a harmless one-line addition. Same scrutiny as the hooks above.
/.github/ @Ardenexal
